# Aya secrets. Copy this file to secrets.env and fill in the values.
#
#   copy secrets.env.template secrets.env
#
# RULES
#   1. secrets.env NEVER leaves this folder.
#   2. This folder is deliberately OUTSIDE OneDrive. The vault syncs to the
#      cloud and is read by an externally hosted model. Secrets must not.
#   3. Never paste a value into a chat, a prompt, or a task description.
#      Aya's prompts reference the NAME on the left, never the value.
#   4. One value per line, no quotes, no spaces around the equals sign.
#
# Fill these two. The rest are for later steps.

# From BotFather. Regenerate first, then paste the NEW token here.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Your own Telegram chat id. Not secret, kept here for portability.
# Message @userinfobot on Telegram to get it.
SARA_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- Step 2 and later, leave blank for now ---

# Discord developer portal, Bot tab, Reset Token.
# This is the ONLY Discord value that is secret. Three chunks split by dots.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# LEAVE THESE TWO BLANK. The verifier fetches them from the token and
# prints them for you. Do not go hunting in the portal.
#
# For reference, if you ever do want them by hand:
#   BOT_USER_ID  = the long 18 or 19 digit number in the developer portal URL
#                  (https://discord.com/developers/applications/<THIS>/bot).
#                  Also shown as Application ID or Client ID. Same value.
#                  NOT the #1234 discriminator after the bot's name.
#   GUILD_ID     = right click the server name with Developer Mode on,
#                  Copy Server ID.
# Neither is secret.
DISCORD_BOT_USER_ID=
DISCORD_GUILD_ID=

# OpenRouter, for running the high frequency sweeps off Claude credit.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
